# Git commits and pull requests

## Do not commit without approval

- **Never** run `git add`, `git commit`, or `git push` unless the user explicitly asks in that conversation.
- "Fix this" or "implement X" is **not** permission to commit — wait for an explicit commit/push request.
- Never amend, force-push, or skip hooks unless the user explicitly requests it.

## Show the commit message before committing

When the user asks to commit:

1. Run `git status` and `git diff` (staged + unstaged) to see what will be included.
2. **Present the proposed commit message** to the user in your reply — do not run `git commit` yet.
3. List the files that will be staged (or ask if anything should be excluded).
4. **Wait for explicit approval** of the message (e.g. "looks good", "commit it", or an edited message).
5. Only then run `git add` and `git commit`.

If the user approves with a different message, use their version.

## Pull requests

- When creating or editing a PR (`gh pr create`, PR body, title), **show the proposed title and body** before opening/updating if the user did not supply exact text.
- PR titles and bodies follow the same attribution rules as commit messages (see below).

## Push

- Never push unless the user explicitly asks.
- After push, confirm branch and remote ref (e.g. `origin/staging`).

## Commit message style

- 1–2 sentences focused on **why**, not a file list.

## No Cursor attribution (commits and PRs)

**Forbidden by default** — do not include unless the user **explicitly approves** that specific text:

- "Made with Cursor", "by Cursor", "via Cursor", or similar product advertising
- Any mention of **Cursor** as the authoring tool, agent, or IDE in commit messages, PR titles, or PR bodies
- Co-authored-by, footers, or badges that advertise Cursor

This applies to `git commit`, `gh pr create`, `gh pr edit`, and any ship/release scripts that embed commit or PR text.

**Allowed without asking:** none of the above.

**Exception:** only if the user explicitly requests Cursor attribution in that message (e.g. "add Made with Cursor to the commit") — use their exact wording, nothing extra.
